
AMISOR borehole AM05 MICROCAT data for 2011/2012 season
-------------------------------------------------------

Data from the first download.

ascii format
------------
contained in column formatted files catxxxx_2.dat, where
xxxx = microcat serial number. The columns are:

1. decimal time - decimal days, where 0.0 = 0000 on January 1st 2001.
So, for example, midday on 15th January 2001 is decimal time 14.5
2. temperature (deg. C, T90)
3. conductivity (mS/cm)
4. pressure (dbar)
5. salinity (PSS78)
6. to 11. day, month, year, hour, minute, second.

* Note that all times are UTC.

* There is a line of data for each recording interval (i.e. no gaps),
and null data is represented by -999.0

* For cat7322, there are conductivity/salinity data spikes at the following times:
(note: not removed from the data)
1630 on 01/09/2011
2030 to 2200 on 25/10/2011
0600 on 25/11/2011

* For cat7327, there are conductivity/salinity data spikes at the following times:
(note: not removed from the data)
1400 on 28/03/2011 to 0530 on 29/03/2011

* For cat7327_2 file version, all pressure (and hence all conductivity and salinity) 
data are bad.

* Clock errors were small (< 26 seconds), and no clock drift corrections have 
been made.

* Mean pressures over this latest download (including all pressure steps):

cat7327 =  580.2 dbar (i.e. point value immediately after deployment in January 2010)
cat7326 =  727.4 dbar
cat7322 =  864.9 dbar

* The pressure steps appear to be real.

* Original pressure data for microcat 7327 are bad. All conductivity and
salinity values are recalculated using a constant pressure value of 580.2 dbar
(the value immediately after deployment in January 2010). These recalculated data
are in the file version cat7327_2meanp. Unexpected salinity/conductivity trends
are evident in the recalculated data, most likely related to real values measured by a frozen-in 
instrument. Note that the other 2 microcats show rapid pressure change events - with no
pressure data for cat7327, it is unknown if this instrument underwent the same changes. As a
result, there may be a further inaccuracy in the recalculated salinity data for cat7327
of up to 0.02 (PSS78) (corresponding to pressure out by 20 dbar).


matlab
------
contained in matlab format files catxxxx_2.mat, where
xxxx = microcat serial number. 



